<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Outer Mongolia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Outer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a> was the northern part of Mongolia under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing dynasty</a>, inhabited mainly by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalkha-mongols">Khalkha Mongols</a>, who submitted to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kangxi-emperor">Kangxi Emperor</a> in 1691. After the fall of the Qing it declared independence in 1911 under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogd-khan">Bogd Khan</a>, and with Soviet support became the Mongolian People's Republic in 1924, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> recognised in 1946. It corresponds to the present state of Mongolia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/outer-mongolia.jpg" alt="Outer Mongolia" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lilauid · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Republic_of_China_edcp_location_map_(disputed_territories)_Mongolia_Area.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
